 enceladus:{title:'Enceladus',kind:'Ocean world · plume-accessible',stance:'Strongest ThermoBase case study — rich access to ocean-derived material does not equal evidence of life.',score:'14/14',scoreLabel:'ordinal compatibility of the hydrogenotrophic pathway',evidence:['Cassini established a global subsurface ocean and sampled its plume','Molecular H₂ is consistent with hydrothermal water–rock chemistry','CH₄, CO₂ and other plume constituents provide a redox/chemical context','Phosphate has been detected in plume material','2025 work found diverse organics in fresh plume ice grains; 2026 work stresses the abiotic baseline'],thermo:'ThermoBase identifies hydrogenotrophic methanogenesis as the leading metabolic hypothesis in the 14-criterion matrix. This is a compatibility result, not a life probability. No single terrestrial organism matches every inferred Enceladus constraint.',sources:D.web_release.planetary_sources.Enceladus},
